## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, on-device NLP that yields actionable summaries from multilingual consumer reviews, a realistic Instacart/Amazon use case, without network dependency.

## Key Concepts
- On-device multilang NLP under tight size constraints
- Feature extraction via lightweight POS or rules
- Sentiment aggregation and justification
- Privacy-first data labeling and offline evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreFeature(feature, sentences) {
  let score = 0;
  for (const s of sentences) {
    if (s.toLowerCase().includes(feature)) {
      if (/\b(good|great|excellent|loved)\b/.test(s)) score += 1;
      if (/\b(bad|worst|terrible|hate)\b/.test(s)) score -= 1;
    }
  }
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle negation and language switch within a single sentence?
- How would you validate usefulness of summaries to buyers?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical on-device NLP with privacy, multilingual support, and simple explanations—core concerns for real-world edge deployments.

## Key Concepts
- On-device inference and privacy preservation
- Multilingual model distillation and language detection
- Pipeline: classify then extract slots
- Lightweight explainability for model decisions
- Offline evaluation with latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
function onDeviceInference(text, model) {
  const lang = detectLanguage(text);
  const category = classifier(lang).predict(text);
  const slots = slotTagger(text);
  const explanation = explain(text, category, slots);
  return { category, slots, explanation };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to handle language-detection errors gracefully?
- How would you measure privacy impact and data leakage risk?

